{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/758043-beast-concept","id":758043,"title":"Beast Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-05T22:48:05-08:00","id":758043,"title":"Beast Concept","content":"Not entirely sure how to stat this out, but I had the thought of building what was very much like a Dresden Files style vampire of the White Court as a Beast (for use as a villain, and am leaning more towards Skavis or Malvora than Raith). I supposing that Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song are the obvious go-to Atavisms, but I'm not sure what Family or Hunger work, nor which Nightmares would support the concept. Maybe the Hunger for Prey? Hunger for Power might also work... hmm. Anyone have any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T20:32:51-08:00","id":765319,"title":"","content":"Well let's see Skavis and Malvora favored fear and despair in their victims, as opposed to the lust/pleasure thing the Raiths do, if I recall correctly. Anakim are a good family fit as part of their thing is making the victim feel utterly powerless and hopeless. Makara are good since you can drive the idea of your prey not having anywhere to go the problems are mounting ever higher and either they can't keep their head above the proverbial waters for long, or they already are under the water and can't find the way to the surface. The Ugallu specialize in knowing everything about the target, you can probably leverage that to your ends as well. I don't think any of the families are out, but those seem the most effective mesh to me.<br /> <br /> Tyrant and Predator are obvious hunger categories as you say. Though depending on how you want to play it a Collector could be viable. A ravager would also work well. Nemesis is a maybe for me, but if you're aiming to use the character as a villain it would probably over complicate things.<br /> <br /> Don't forget Needs Must that's a useful atavism for finding prey.<br /> <br /> Nightmares are probably going to be more your bread and butter here than atavisms. I mean no self respecting member of the White Court would actually do their work on their own after-all. I think we'll need a bit more on how you plan to have the villain operate before we can recommend some good nightmares though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}